   168	/**
   169	 * Telegram methods deliberately classified as carrying NO reader-visible field.
   170	 *
   171	 * Added 2026-08-10 on a round-3 convergence finding, and it closes the last version of this window's
   172	 * defining hole. Before it, the classification was open-world: a method in the map was guarded, and
   173	 * EVERYTHING ELSE was silently unguarded — so a future `sendPhoto` with a caption, or a `sendPoll` with a
   174	 * question, would join the codebase completely unclassified and no check would say a word. Unclassified
   175	 * members silently escaping a population is the exact shape that has produced this branch's every repeat
   176	 * failure.
   177	 *
   178	 * With both lists present the world is CLOSED: every Telegram method a sender calls is either guarded or
   179	 * explicitly declared bodyless. That closure is now enforced by `src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts`,
   180	 * which REFUSES a method in neither list — "review required", not "assumed safe".
