   486	 * Counting a destination as content is precisely how the original incident shipped: a payload whose only
   487	 * visible characters lived inside a URL. This now falls out of the table rather than being a rule applied
   488	 * beside it.
   489	 *
   490	 * A `mathematical_expression` is LaTeX SOURCE. Its source characters are not its rendered glyphs — a
   491	 * spacing-only expression is all letters and paints nothing — so it is marked OPAQUE rather than counted
   492	 * as visible. That is the honest position: this guard cannot decide a formula, it can only decline to let
   493	 * one vouch for an otherwise-invisible message.
