The first decisive point is already visible: the scan distinguishes “proven empty” from “opaque,” but the assertion still allows both because `leaves.length === 0` returns. That is a real gap, but it is explicitly in the stated-open list, so I will report it only in regression-check—not inflate the new-finding count. I’m now auditing the transcription for additional, genuinely new mismatches.
