docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass42-verdict.md:77:- **`answerCallbackQuery` / `editForumTopic`:** Still open at [invisible-payload.ts:117](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:117). Telegram documents displayed callback text and empty forum names preserving the current name: [answerCallbackQuery](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#answercallbackquery), [editForumTopic](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#editforumtopic).
docs/audits/phase-b/family-review-2026-08-07/review-building.txt:232:**In practice.** Since 2026-07-09 the attention queue's DEFAULT routing is single-topic: every item — all priorities, HIGH/URGENT included — posts as a message into the ONE durable "🔔 Attention" hub topic and never spawns a per-item forum topic (`attentionRouting.mode: 'per-item'` is the legacy opt-out). Beneath that default sit three structural layers, all still enforced for the legacy mode and for every non-attention caller: (1) emitters aggregate — a detector that finds N problems emits ONE item carrying the count and the list (`AgentWorktreeDetector.runDetection` is the canonical pattern); (2) the shaper — `AttentionTopicGuard` budgets per-source + globally at `createAttentionItem` and coalesces overflow into one notice topic; (3) the backstop — `createForumTopic` itself (the one place topics are born) enforces a last-resort auto-topic ceiling on every caller, current and future, with `origin: 'auto'` as the DEFAULT so a feature that never heard of the budget is still bounded; only explicit `user` (humans are self-rate-limiting) and `system` (fixed-cardinality create-once topics) are exempt. The burst-invariant test fires 1,000 synthetic notifications through the REAL pipeline with shipped-default budgets and fails the build if more than the budget of topics get created; the funnel lint refuses raw `createForumTopic` API calls outside the budgeted funnel.
docs/audits/phase-b/family-review-2026-08-07/review-building.txt:238:**Applied through.** The `topicCreationBudget` ceiling inside `TelegramAdapter.createForumTopic` (origin-typed: `user`/`system`/`auto`, auto-by-default); `AttentionTopicGuard` at `createAttentionItem` (the 2026-05-28 shaper, kept); aggregate emission in `AgentWorktreeDetector`; `tests/integration/notification-flood-burst-invariant.test.ts` (the build-failing burst proof, shipped-default budgets); `scripts/lint-no-unfunneled-topic-creation.js` in `pnpm lint` (no raw `createForumTopic` API calls outside the funnel). Registered as **P17** in `docs/INSTAR-DESIGN-PRINCIPLES-AND-LESSONS.md`.
docs/audits/phase-b/family-review-2026-08-07/review-building.txt:246:**In practice.** The default destination for an ownerless notice IS the alerts/hub topic (this agent: 7848) — routing there is the RULE, not a fallback the code happens to reach. Since 2026-07-09 this is enforced at the attention chokepoint itself: `createAttentionItem` defaults to single-topic routing, posting EVERY item — HIGH/URGENT included — into the ONE "🔔 Attention" hub topic (per-item topics survive only behind the `attentionRouting.mode: 'per-item'` legacy opt-out). A feature that notifies per-element over a collection must AGGREGATE (one summary item carrying the count + the list), never one item per element. The bounding machinery beneath remains: `TelegramAdapter.createForumTopic` enforces a last-resort budget on every automatically-created topic (`origin: 'auto'` by default — the layer that cannot be dodged by giving each item a unique source, the fix after the 2026-06-05 worktree-detector flood); `AttentionTopicGuard` coalesces non-critical items from a flooding source in legacy mode; and `notification-flood-burst-invariant.test.ts` holds the bound at build time.
docs/audits/phase-b/family-review-2026-08-07/review-building.txt:252:**Applied through.** The single-topic default at the routing chokepoint itself — `TelegramAdapter.createAttentionItem` routes every item into the "🔔 Attention" hub unless `attentionRouting.mode: 'per-item'` opts out (shipped 2026-07-09; the enforcement build this entry previously tracked); the `topicCreationBudget` ceiling inside `TelegramAdapter.createForumTopic` (origin-typed, auto-by-default) + `AttentionTopicGuard` at `createAttentionItem` + `tests/integration/notification-flood-burst-invariant.test.ts` — the existing *Bounded Notification Surface* machinery, which this standard makes load-bearing for routing. This registry entry + its **P23** twin in `docs/INSTAR-DESIGN-PRINCIPLES-AND-LESSONS.md` fire the `/spec-converge` lessons-aware reviewer on any feature that would create a topic per alert.
docs/audits/phase-b/family-review-2026-08-07/review-building.txt:268:**Applied through.** The closed `origin:'system'` bypass in `TelegramAdapter.createForumTopic` (only `origin:'user'` or a declared `bounded:true` create-once topic is exempt) + the critical-item flood bound in `createAttentionItem`, both shipped in this pass and pinned by `tests/integration/notification-flood-burst-invariant.test.ts`; the two volume/routing standards above (which this one sits atop); and — the enforcement now unlocked by ratification (tracked `<!-- tracked: CMT-1901 -->`) — a `/spec-converge` disposition reviewer that asks Question 1 ("could the agent just DO this?") of any new user-facing emitter, plus a lint that flags a new proactive `sendToTopic`/`createAttentionItem` emitter that ships enabled-by-default without a stated human-needs-it justification.
