docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass43-full.md:11:The principal new bypass is that Telegram’s `editMessageText` accepts reader-visible `rich_message` content without `text`, while the door checks only `text` and returns silently when it is absent. [Telegram documentation](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#editmessagetext)
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass47.out:15:   [invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:125) classifies `sendRichMessage` and `sendRichMessageDraft` as accepting alternative fields `text` and `rich_message`. They do not: the live API requires only `rich_message` for both methods ([sendRichMessage](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#sendrichmessage), [sendRichMessageDraft](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#sendrichmessagedraft)), and the server reads only `rich_message` ([official implementation](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api/blob/master/telegram-bot-api/Client.cpp#L11607-L11619)).
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass47.out:19:   Concrete failure path: a rich-message request supplies a harmless visible query `text` and carries the actual reader-invisible `rich_message` in a byte-oriented JSON body. The door treats unsupported `text` as decisive, never inspects the body, and sends it; Telegram ignores `text` and consumes `rich_message`.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass47.out:71:- **`editForumTopic`:** Still guarded unconditionally through `name`; empty-name/preserve-current semantics remain unmodeled ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:140)).
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass47.out:73:- **Local Bot API Server:** Still outside runtime and lint recognition because both hard-code `api.telegram.org` ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:60), [lint](/Users/justin/window12-exam/scripts/lint-telegram-egress-boundary.mjs:48)). Telegram supports replacing the cloud endpoint with a [local server](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api#moving-a-bot-to-a-local-server).
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass47.out:81:- **Structured content only in JSON bodies:** Still open. Query/form/multipart collection leaves `rich_message` as a JSON-serialized string, after which JSON punctuation satisfies the scalar predicate.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass47.out:83:- **Cross-field query/body precedence:** Still open and unsafe. The waiver uses `fields.some(...)` ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:389)), but Telegram’s `editMessageText` chooses `rich_message` whenever present before falling back to `text` ([official implementation](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api/blob/master/telegram-bot-api/Client.cpp#L13605-L13612)).
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass47.out:89:- **Normalized host spellings in lint:** Still open. The prefilter and recognizer depend on literal `api.telegram.org/` source text rather than URL semantics ([lint](/Users/justin/window12-exam/scripts/lint-telegram-egress-boundary.mjs:51)).
