docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass30-verdict.md:32:   Unicode defines category `M` as graphic and permits isolated combining characters to be presented graphically as base characters; representative charts show them visibly. [Unicode Standard, Chapter 3](https://www.unicode.org/versions/Unicode17.0.0/core-spec/chapter-3/). The spec honestly narrows its guarantee to “mechanically-visible” ([spec:196](/Users/justin_instar_1/.instar/agents/echo/.worktrees/guard-effectiveness-observability/docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.md:196)), but its product intent remains reader visibility. The new definition over-refuses real graphic content.
