docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass37-verdict.md:19:5. **DESIGN — Multipart is over-refused on a false “cannot read without consuming” premise.** `FormData`, `Blob`, and `ArrayBuffer` are grouped with one-shot streams and categorically rejected at [telegram-egress.ts:119](/Users/justin_instar_1/.instar/agents/echo/.worktrees/guard-effectiveness-observability/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:119)-[122](/Users/justin_instar_1/.instar/agents/echo/.worktrees/guard-effectiveness-observability/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:122); the test repeats the premise at [telegram-egress-boundary.test.ts:92](/Users/justin_instar_1/.instar/agents/echo/.worktrees/guard-effectiveness-observability/tests/unit/telegram-egress-boundary.test.ts:92)-[101](/Users/justin_instar_1/.instar/agents/echo/.worktrees/guard-effectiveness-observability/tests/unit/telegram-egress-boundary.test.ts:101). Native `FormData` is iterable without consuming it, while `Blob` and `ArrayBuffer` are repeatably readable. Failure path: a legitimate multipart `sendMessage` carrying visible text is rejected before the network, despite being checkable.
