   153	## What changed since pass 44
   154	
   155	**Structured fields are walked to their TEXT LEAVES.** `rich_message` is an `InputRichMessage`, not a
   156	string; the previous repair named the field in the closed-world table and then checked it with a string
   157	test, so the table read as covering a field nothing inspected. Leaves are gathered from `html`,
   158	`markdown`, and any nested `text`, with each leaf's format taken from its KEY rather than the request's
   159	`parse_mode`. One visible leaf delivers; all-invisible refuses; no leaves is undecidable and allowed.
   160	Urls, ids and type tags are deliberately not gathered.
   161	
   162	**Also still open from pass 44 and NOT claimed:** the Local Bot API Server endpoint is outside both method
   163	recognition and the boundary lint; the multipart, single-read, live-method-table and documentation claims
   164	that reading called false.
   165	
   166	**The pattern to attack:** twice now a repair has been the right idea in the wrong SHAPE, and in both
   167	cases the artefact that was supposed to prove coverage (a test, a closed-world table entry) was what made
   168	the gap invisible. Look for coverage that is asserted by structure rather than exercised by behaviour.
